{"ld": 1023, "paper": "SP441", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Reestablish the Blue Economy Task Force to Support Maine's Emergence as a Center for Blue Economy Innovation and Opportunity in the 21st Century (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "s-duson-jill", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bennett-richard", "h-hepler-allison", "s-lawrence-mark", "s-moore-marianne", "s-reny-cameron", "h-rielly-morgan", "h-stover-holly", "s-talbot-ross-rachel"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This resolve reestablishes the Blue Economy Task Force, which was previously established by the 131st Legislature in 2023. The task force is charged with developing a report that outlines the sectors of the State's blue economy and existing economic development plans or strategies for blue economy sectors and identifies opportunities where the State can enhance or facilitate the growth and scaling of blue economy businesses, including the creation of a design for a proposed Center for a Blue Economy. The task force is required to submit a written report by February 1, 2026 to the Governor and the Joint Standing Committee on Housing and Economic Development, which may report out legislation based on the findings and recommendations in the report to the Second Regular Session of the 132nd Legislature.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0441&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-07-01", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-07-01"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN102302.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1023)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0441&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-297)", "u